  "ssml": "<speak version=\"1.0\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis\" xmlns:mstts=\"https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts\" xml:lang=\"en-PH\">\n  <voice name=\"en-PH-RosaNeural\">\n    <mstts:express-as style=\"cheerful\">\n      <prosody rate=\"102%\" pitch=\"+4%\">\n        Finally, <break time=\"300ms\"/> Step 3! <break time=\"550ms\"/> Let&apos;s plug the word <emphasis level=\"moderate\">pristine</emphasis> into our bridge sentence. <break time=\"550ms\"/> <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Pristine</emphasis> means clean and pure. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Which word means the exact same thing as <emphasis level=\"moderate\">pristine</emphasis>? <break time=\"650ms\"/> <break time=\"800ms\"/> <emphasis level=\"moderate\">Unspoiled</emphasis>! <break time=\"550ms\"/> <phoneme alphabet=\"ipa\" ph=\"ˈtræŋkwɪl\">Tranquil</phoneme> is to calm, <break time=\"300ms\"/> as <emphasis level=\"moderate\">pristine</emphasis> is to <emphasis level=\"moderate\">unspoiled</emphasis>. <break time=\"550ms\"/> Nice! <break time=\"550ms\"/> You nailed it.\n      </prosody>\n    </mstts:express-as>\n  </voice>\n</speak>",
